{"title":"2020 Mock Combo AMC 10 II Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>To begin, since we know that aa, bb, cc are indistinguishable, then we can just use complementary counting. \n</p><p>Since they are indistinguishable, then one of the way to arrange them so that no two adjacent letters are identical would be ABCABC, which there are 3!*3!\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018013147\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.002 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.003 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 1/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20869:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018013147 and revision id 147369. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}